Completed one bounded non-UI release-proof sprint for Full-Stack MVP sequence item 9: US-112 Hosted CI run proof collector.

Changed:
- Added `scripts/hosted-ci-proof.mjs`, a read-only GitHub Actions evidence collector using `gh run list`.
- Added `npm run proof:hosted-ci`.
- Added `docs/stories/US-112-hosted-ci-run-proof-collector.md`.
- Updated `docs/stories/backlog.md`, `docs/product/runtime-architecture.md`, and `docs/TEST_MATRIX.md`.
- Wrote sprint evidence to `.claude/sprint-runs/round-186-20260519-hosted-ci-proof-collector.log`.
- Generated `reports/hosted-ci-proof.json`.

Validation run:
- `npm run proof:hosted-ci` completed and wrote `reports/hosted-ci-proof.json` with `status=blocked`.
  - Exact blocker: `no_successful_hosted_ci_run_found`.
  - `gh run list` succeeded read-only, but the only recent hosted workflow run found was cancelled.
- `npm run validate:quick` passed: 57 test files, 548 tests.
- `npm run smoke:routes` passed for `/`, `/login`, `/join/ALPHA01`, `/dashboard`, and `/instructor/dashboard`.

Gap reduced:
- Hosted CI proof is no longer just an undocumented missing item; the repo now has a repeatable, non-mutating collector/report path for hosted GitHub Actions evidence.
- Actual successful hosted CI proof remains pending until `local-release-validation.yml` has a completed successful hosted run.

No commit, push, PR, hosted workflow dispatch, deployment, Supabase mutation, Inngest mutation, or Vercel mutation was performed.

Recommended next iteration:
- After a successful hosted `local-release-validation.yml` run exists, rerun `npm run proof:hosted-ci` to turn the report from `blocked` to `passed`; otherwise select the next safe release/platform proof slice that does not require unavailable hosted provider credentials.

